    {
      "text": "Jacob begat Joseph the husband of Mary, Matt. 1:16. Jesus saith unto her, Go, call thy husband, John 4:16. bound by the law to her husband … but if the husband be dead, Rom. 7:2. let every woman have her own husband, 1 Cor. 7:2. husband render unto the wife due benevolence, 1 Cor. 7:3. woman which hath an husband that believeth not, 1 Cor. 7:13. unbelieving husband is sanctified by the wife, 1 Cor. 7:14 (D&C 74:1). how she may please her husband, 1 Cor. 7:34. Wives, submit yourselves unto your own husbands, Eph. 5:22 (Col. 3:18). husband is the head of the wife, Eph. 5:23. Husbands, love your wives, Eph. 5:25 (Col. 3:19). wife see that she reverence her husband, Eph. 5:33. bishop … the husband of one wife, 1 Tim. 3:2 (Titus 1:6). young women to be sober, to love their husbands, Titus 2:4. obedient to their own husbands, Titus 2:5. ye wives, be in subjection to your own husbands, 1 Pet. 3:1. ye husbands, dwell with them according to knowledge, 1 Pet. 3:7. prepared as a bride adorned for her husband, Rev. 21:2.",
